A||||5||lennyb4||Freakin' Reverse||||8||
Z||000000||lennyb4||04-14-2000||09:21 AM||||Heres one for ya.. Sometimes (more like 90% of the time) i have a very hard time getting into reverse. I normally have to try twice (the first time it normally grinds). Also my clutch engages about 2-3" off the floor. Ive bleed the system (2x),and it doesnt look like my petals bent. Other then that it rides and shifts fine..Any ideas..||||reg||8
Z||000001||iplayazi||04-14-2000||10:47 AM||||I dont know much about fiero clutches but I have a brother that has a 92 rscamaro and it grinds when he puts it in reverse.. what he does is when he wants to go in reverse he puts it into third then reverse.. I guess it helped him out.. try it out||||reg||1
Z||000002||fieroshop||04-14-2000||10:57 AM||||If what ipayazi does not work then you may have the same problem that I had. Several years ago before I opened up shop.I had my clutch replaced on my 88 GT. I had no choice as to what clutch they put in as I was traveling on vacation and needed to get going well as it turned out I did everything that you did and I finally decided to pull the tranny and I found that on this clutch the throwout bearing had worn a groove in the fingers of the pressure plate and the release of the clutch once we measured was a good 60 thousand of an inch lower then even stock oem clutches. Meaning that the clutch would engage just of the floor nad if trying to shift I could not unless I stopped the engine. But it started out by hard shifting into reverse then first and finally all gears.||||reg||1
Z||000003||lennyb4||04-14-2000||01:07 PM||||I just bought a new CenterForce II kit i just have to find someone to install it. What about the clutch fork? I heard these can get bent or wore-out over time. Should i consider replacing this when the clutch gets done? Believe it or not i still have the original clutch (90,000 miles) in the car. Its not really slipping yet, just a pain to shift..||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||04-14-2000||02:24 PM||||if you do get a new fork get it from NAPA.. not the fiero store.. it's like $100 from the fiero store.. I got my new (VERY nice) fork from NAPA for $60.. and $5 for the 2 new bushings and one new bushing cap... PAIN IN THE BUTT to get the bushing out.. may take an hour or so just don't give up... ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fiasco||04-14-2000||08:40 PM||||I know I was taught to always throw it into a forward gear before reverse- on any manual tranny. This stops the shaft from spinning before you try to make it spin the other direction.<BR>As for the clutch, mine starts to engage at about 1 1/2 from the floor and always has... I can't imagine that it's supposed to be higher than that- is it?  Although I do still have the orig. aluminum pedal, I don't think it's bent more than 1/4".||||reg||2
